<title>UK: Bank of Melbourne ups one-year FRN to $200 million.</title>
<headline>Bank of Melbourne ups one-year FRN to $200 million.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue has been increased, lead manager Nomura said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK OF MELBOURNE LTD</p>
<p> AMT  * $200 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY    21.NOV.97</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     FLAT	PAY DATE    21.NOV.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A-	  ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   5 BP</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A3	  REOFFER    PAR</p>
<p> NOTES    * ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED ON 01.NOV.96 FOR $150 MLN</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/UK/AU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.025 BP  SELL CONC  0.025 BP</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
